{
  "version": 1,
  "$howToUse": [
    "Every sprite the app can draw is declared here by a stable key. The renderer only ever asks for keys.",
    "A sprite gets its pixels from one of three source kinds, and can switch between them at any time without touching app code:",
    "  sheet     - one cell lifted straight out of a vendor sheet",
    "  composite - a kitbash: several cells stacked with offsets, flips, and tints",
    "  file      - a hand-authored PNG in assets/sprites/authored/",
    "Start everything as composite. When a component can't be kitbashed convincingly, draw it and flip that",
    "one entry to 'file'. Nothing else changes. That is the whole migration path.",
    "",
    "THEME KEYS: tokens starting with @ bake as reserved key colors and are swapped per room at draw time.",
    "  @mask-dark  @mask-light  @signal",
    "Use them for anything that should take on the room's color. Use literal tokens (copper, silk, ok, warn,",
    "fault) for anything that must look identical in every room.",
    "",
    "Run `npm run assets:bake` after editing. It writes assets/atlas/ and then the purity validator checks it.",
    "To pick cell coordinates, render a ruled contact sheet first — never guess:",
    "  node tools/sheet-contact.mjs k1bit out.png --zoom 6 --range 0,6,22,16"
  ],
  "sheets": {
    "k1bit": {
      "file": "vendor/kenney_1-bit-pack/Tilesheet/monochrome-transparent.png",
      "cell": {
        "w": 16,
        "h": 16,
        "marginX": 0,
        "marginY": 0,
        "spacingX": 1,
        "spacingY": 1
      },
      "$verified": [
        "2026-09-09 — measured, not assumed. 832x373 px. Empty seam rows land at y=16,33,50,67,... = 16+17k,",
        "which is exactly what cell 16 + spacing 1 predicts, and 16/1/0 is the only exact tiling of 832x373.",
        "Grid is 49 x 22 cells. Agrees with Tilesheet.txt shipped in the pack.",
        "The sheet holds exactly 2 colours: transparent and rgb(249,250,251). Tint every layer and it is",
        "palette-clean by construction. See assets/vendor/kenney_1-bit-pack/SOURCE.md."
      ]
    },
    "k1bit_color": {
      "file": "vendor/kenney_1-bit-pack/Tilesheet/colored-transparent.png",
      "cell": {
        "w": 16,
        "h": 16,
        "marginX": 0,
        "marginY": 0,
        "spacingX": 1,
        "spacingY": 1
      },
      "$verified": "2026-09-09 — 832x373, same 49 x 22 grid and same cell order as k1bit. 8 colours.",
      "$note": "Unused. Everything gets recoloured anyway, so the 2-colour monochrome sheet is strictly less work. Needs an 8-entry remap table before any layer can reference it without an explicit tint."
    },
    "rgs_gray": {
      "file": "vendor/FreeTopDownTilesetPixelArt-CC0/Tilesheet/tileset_gray.png",
      "cell": {
        "w": 16,
        "h": 16,
        "marginX": 0,
        "marginY": 0,
        "spacingX": 0,
        "spacingY": 0
      },
      "$verified": "2026-09-09 — 256x80, no gutters, exact 16 x 5 grid. 19 colours, 8-bit RGBA.",
      "$note": "Substrate speckle only, and not before M2. Needs a remap table — a flat tint would erase the speckle that is the only reason to reach for this pack."
    }
  },
  "$sheetsDeliberatelyAbsent": {
    "kenney_ui-pack-space-expansion": "740 loose PNGs, no grid, 33 colours with semi-transparent edges, rounded/glossy grammar. DOM chrome only, never the atlas. See its SOURCE.md.",
    "OpenGameArt-cc0oga": "Wrong silhouette grammar at 30 colours; three of its sheets have no alpha at all. Two files in it are license-untraceable and are blocked by validate-assets.mjs. See its SOURCE.md."
  },
