  "$decorNote": [
    "decor.* keys are the aesthetic furniture of the board: vias, screws, junctions, grilles,",
    "pad arrays, fiducials and indicator LEDs. Cut from the Kenney 1-bit sheet, which is 2 colours",
    "(transparent + white), so tinting a layer makes it palette-clean by construction.",
    "",
    "Cell coordinates were read off a ruled contact sheet, never guessed:",
    "  node tools/sheet-contact.mjs k1bit out.png --zoom 10 --range 14,0,22,7",
    "",
    "Every tint here is a LITERAL token, never an @theme key. The theme-key swap is not implemented",
    "in the renderer yet and an @token would bake as reserved magenta. It is also simply correct:",
    "these are the shared tri-tone and the status colours, which do not change between rooms."
  ]
}
